      "message": "Could the message say what fails without this patch? As far as I can see, aosp/4312509 already dumps 4KB slices and writes NT_FILE in 4KB units with slice offsets, so what is left is the 16KB data alignment and `p_align` in the core of a 4KB process. The subject could say so too, e.g. \"ANDROID: P3S: coredump: Align ELF core segments to the process page size\".\n\nAlso, as on aosp/4367956, would you mind moving `elf_core_p3s.c` from aosp/4367986 into this patch? As far as I can see, its PT_LOAD alignment check is the one that fails without it.",
