      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T21:29:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that the core of a 4KB process needs this: its PT_LOAD segments start at 4KB boundaries, but `ELF_EXEC_PAGESIZE` has been `PAGE_SIZE_KERNEL` on arm64 since aosp/4312470, so `p_offset` and `p_vaddr` don\u0027t always agree modulo the 16KB `p_align`.\n\nCould this and the `p_align` hunk use `ELF_MIN_ALIGN` instead of `mm_pte_size(current-\u003emm)`? With `CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE` it is `PAGE_SIZE`, which already follows the dumping process in this file, and otherwise it stays `ELF_EXEC_PAGESIZE`:\n\n```\n\tdataoff \u003d offset \u003d roundup(offset, ELF_MIN_ALIGN);\n\t...\n\t\tphdr.p_align \u003d ELF_MIN_ALIGN;\n```\n\nThat keeps x86_64 page size emulation as it is. There `ELF_EXEC_PAGESIZE` is the emulated `__PAGE_SIZE` (4568e574ede8, \"ANDROID: 16K: x86_64: Set ELF_EXEC_PAGESIZE to __PAGE_SIZE\"), while `mm_pte_size()` is the 4KB kernel page, so this would change the alignment of emulated 16KB cores.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "02a7022f3b0bea4dadbc6c054234e9b3bcfdfb2a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
