      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T21:29:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the `fs/coredump.c` hunks don\u0027t change anything. aosp/4312509 opted this file into `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e`, so `PAGE_SIZE` and `PAGE_SHIFT` here are already `mm_pte_size()` and `mm_pte_shift()` of `current-\u003emm` (no remote mm is set during a dump), and `size` is always `PAGE_SIZE`. `dump_user_range()` already steps by 4KB in a 4KB process and writes each slice from the `page_offset` that `get_dump_page()` returns, which also sets it to 0 first.\n\nThe same goes for `data[1]` in `fill_files_note()`: `fs/binfmt_elf.c` has opted in since aosp/4312470, so `PAGE_SIZE` there is already the page size that `m-\u003epgoff` counts in.\n\nWould it be OK to drop these hunks and keep only the alignment change in `elf_core_dump()`?",
